  "slug": "diploid-dipler-f8ab",
  "summary": "Single-cell and multiomic QTL maps now resolve variant effects by cell type, chromatin context, and repeat structure across immune and disease datasets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving genetic effects on gene regulation by cell type and chromatin context. TenK10K phase 1 maps common and rare variant effects on immune gene expression across 28 cell types in over 5 million single cells, while a multiomic meta-analysis of 1.7M tandem repeats in 5.4M immune cells maps repeat effects on cell-type expression and chromatin. scATAC-seq of 3.5M PBMCs from 1,042 donors maps caQTLs, and a graph neural network links peaks to genes using QTL layers. scMRdb pairs 5206 GWAS summary statistics with 585 sc-eQTL datasets for cell-type-resolved Mendelian randomization, and a genotype-by-rhythm cosinor framework finds 167 circadian eQTLs across 28 tissues. What is new is explicit inclusion of tandem repeats and cell-type context within association frameworks. The CADD-annotated pipeline, VarNexus, and MetabDB are narrower annotation and resource applications.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
